@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Local synthetic conversation fixture
+
+The opt-in local test route `/app/synthetic-conversation` is mounted inside the existing app router and shell; the review start page links to it only when Vite runs in development with `VITE_SYNTHETIC_CONVERSATION=true`. The standalone fixture entry remains available for comparison. Neither entry is an authorized production feature. The route and UI are disabled in production builds and when the flag is absent.
+
+The route uses the isolated synthetic PostgreSQL prototype `/workspace/work/finance-conversation-synthetic` commit `9acb5b1e5cc509b3f6f6637cf9e77f8f795d74e9`. Vite enables the same-origin `/synthetic-conversations` proxy only in serve mode with the flag and an HTTP `127.0.0.1` `CONVERSATION_FIXTURE_TARGET`. The browser explicitly selects a per-tab synthetic actor; the client sends that fixture identity and the proxy forwards it. With no selected identity, the UI stays signed out and the backend returns 401. Switching actors or using the synthetic logout remounts the screen and clears the visible conversation. These headers are user-controlled test data, not real authentication. The conversation selector is independent of the Journal fixture token and does not establish shared application logout or identity switching. Use only synthetic data. Answers are fixed fixture text; PolicyGuard and output validation are not connected.
+
+From the FE repository, `node integration-fixtures/conversation/verify.mjs` starts disposable local PostgreSQL, backend and loopback Vite, navigates from `/app`, and runs Chromium temporary/opt-in/save/backend restart/resume/delete, then removes the container. It requires the referenced backend candidate with `npm ci` in `local-conversation`, Docker image `postgres:16-alpine`, installed FE dependencies and `/usr/bin/chromium`; it binds Vite port 5179. `node integration-fixtures/conversation/verify-disabled.mjs` checks flag-off navigation and direct route on port 5180. The browser checks switching between synthetic owners and tenants and synthetic logout; the backend verifier additionally covers fixture scope and idempotency. In the shared dependency test environment font files generated Vite filesystem warnings; the functionality test passed.
+
+This does not establish real identity authorization, production migration or retention, provider validation, recovery, or production readiness. The test proxy and route must remain unavailable in production.
